messages:
mia-support: Hey folks — escalating ticket #2341 from Acme. They get a 400 when the model issues a tool call. Customer error: \"schema validation failed: enum field \\\"urgent\\\" had unexpected value \\\"Yes\\\"\". Request id req_0a1b2c3d, model returned a tool_call payload that fails our server-side validator. Root time 2026-03-16T17:12:30Z.

raj-eng: Can you paste the raw request and which model/version? also does the model return args as an object or string? :eyes:

mia-support: Raw request (redacted) below. Model: gpt-compat-1. Payload shows both casing and stringified args issues.
```json
{
  "tool_call": {
    "name": "SendEmail",
    "arguments": "{\"to\": \"bob@acme.com\", \"urgent\": \"Yes\"}"
  }
}
```

alex-platform: Thanks. Two compatibility problems visible: 1) `arguments` is a JSON string instead of an object, 2) `urgent` enum/flag uses \"Yes\" (capital Y) instead of lowercase/boolean our schema expects. Both can trigger our OpenAI-compat validator. Quick repro: fetch raw request from our API logs: 
```bash
curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $REDWOOD_API_KEY" \
  "https://console.redwood.ai/api/v1/requests/req_0a1b2c3d/raw" -o raw.json
jq . raw.json
```

lina-ops: Suggested mitigation: implement a compat normalizer on the request path that: 
- accepts stringified `arguments` and JSON.parse()s them when valid,
- normalizes enum/boolean-ish values (e.g. `Yes`/`YES`/`true`/`1` -> true; `No`/`no`/`false`/`0` -> false),
- lowercases enum strings before validation for known tool schemas. Pseudocode: 
```js
if (typeof payload.tool_call.arguments === 'string') {
  try { payload.tool_call.arguments = JSON.parse(payload.tool_call.arguments) } catch(e) { /* fall through, leave error for validation */ }
}
const normalizeBoolish = v => {
  if (typeof v !== 'string') return v;
  const s = v.toLowerCase();
  if (['yes','true','1','y'].includes(s)) return true;
  if (['no','false','0','n'].includes(s)) return false;
  return v;
}
if (payload.tool_call?.arguments?.urgent !== undefined) {
  payload.tool_call.arguments.urgent = normalizeBoolish(payload.tool_call.arguments.urgent);
}
```

raj-eng: That looks good. Two follow-ups: 1) Do we have a list of tool schemas so normalizer only applies to known fields (to avoid accidental coercion)? 2) Does this run inline (blocking) or as a pre-validator stage that returns a richer error if parsing fails?

alex-platform: For (1) yes — we have per-route/tool schemas in the model catalog. Normalizer should consult the tool schema whitelist to only coerce fields marked as `compat:true`. For (2) run inline before schema validation so callers get corrected payloads where safe; still log incidents where we mutated values. We'll gate the feature behind a per-customer compatibility flag at first.

mia-support: Customer asked for timeline — can we do a hotfix? This is blocking a prod flow for them.

lina-ops: We can roll a hotfix to the compat normalizer on the hosting layer in ~4 hours: patch + canary + rollback. Deploy-bot: canary window scheduled. :hourglass_flowing_sand:

deploy-bot: deploy/start canary for compat-normalizer-hotfix -> 2165436800

alex-platform: I'll prepare a short regression check in the evals harness to include cases: stringified arguments, `Yes`/`YES`/`y`/`1`, and enum-case differences. Also update docs snippet in Console (route-level flag).

mia-support: Great — pls post back when canary finishes. I'll notify Acme and share a temporary workaround: have the model output booleans and objects (we provided the prompt hint). :thumbsup:
